{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1531765-chronicle-of-shadow-fantasy-shard","id":1531765,"title":"Chronicle of Shadow (Fantasy Shard)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-29T20:36:53-08:00","id":1531765,"title":"Chronicle of Shadow (Fantasy Shard)","content":"Inspired by Lostlight Fantasy Chronicle of Darkness.<br /> <br /> <b>Chronicia</b> is what the inhabitant call the world in which they live in. <b><b>C</b></b><b>hronicia</b> is large and unexplore, calling for explorer and adventurer to discover what is hidden within it's shadow, but the shadow threatened to consume those who dare seek it.<br /> <br /> There is 7 Continent in <b><b>C</b></b><b>hronicia</b>, three of which are connerstone of civilization, two of them are mostly primal wild, and one of them use to host a great civilization until most of it sink into the ocean.<br /> <br /> <b>Classica</b> (or the European inspire one) host both the oldest and newest civilization on <b>Chronicia</b>, fuel both by ancient gudge and new revolutionary idea, the people and culture of <b>Classica</b> is a strange mix between both modernity and ancient tradition.<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire</b><br /> At the Center of <b>Classica</b> is <b>Empire of Cain</b>: The <b>Empire of Cain</b> was one the four founding Empire of <b>Classica</b>, it's founding emperor was <b>Cain the First Vampire</b> or that is the legend that the Empire tell, in truth no one really know who founded the Empire, since Vampire who would know that information, are either dead or crazy. The <b>Empire of Cain</b> was once a Great Empire that span across <b>Chronica</b>, but it got into conflict with the three founding Empire causing it downfall. Now what remain of the once Great Empire is held together by it's religion and the remaining great house that rule it.<br /> <br /> North of <b>Empire of Cain</b> is <b>Theocracy of The Beast</b>: A nation establish after four empire war of <b>Classica</b>, the <b>Theocracy of The Beast</b> is rule by the Church of Repentence, who see Vampirism as agent of God to herd humanity to salvation, feed on those who are unworthy, and embrace those who have potential. Recently there have been a new religious movement within the nation, The Crone Army as they called it, they see Vampirism as Divinity itself, and it's their right to do whatever they want with their power. This have cause some tension within the nation, as some part of the country have been converted into The Crone Army, the people of the country hope that a civil war will not occur between the two.<br /> <br /> North of <b>Theocracy of The Beast </b>is <b>Republic of Dragon</b>: One of the newest nation in <b>Classica</b>, the island that the nation is locate in use to be a hub of piracy and revolutionary, until The Great Draconus come to the island and unite the fracture island with his technology. But now the <b>Republic of Dragon</b> the rich upper-class scientist, engineer, and inventor, with the working class worker, farmer, and student. While <b>Republic of Dragon</b> have some religion, it's more focus on the scientific invention and scholraly pursuit making one of the top five most technologically advance nation in <b>Chronicia</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28270,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","user":"Yumlum","date":". 02-29-2024, 11:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T12:24:41-08:00","id":1531793,"title":"","content":"If you're making a kingdom in Requiem I would probably avoid the name Caine along with associated spellings, to avoid confusion with Masquerade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-02T05:18:11-08:00","id":1531841,"title":"","content":"Wasn't Cain something that also exist in Requiem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-02T05:37:39-08:00","id":1531843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1531765-chronicle-of-shadow-fantasy-shard?p=1531841#post1531841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't Cain something that also exist in Requiem?</div> </div> </div> </div>The material in Requiem for Rome includes a heretical doctrine that, after being marked by God as unable to die and unable to be harmed by humanity, Cain conveyed the will of God to several prophets, including Jesus and the vampire Longinus, to prepare the living for consumption by the dead.<br /> <br /> Centuries later, this survives in the Hunter conspiracy known as the Cainite Heresy, who use specially prepared phials of blood to perform ritual magic that they deliberately and willfully do not investigate the origins of and famously use &quot;Who is Cain?&quot; as a sort of calling card.<br /> <br /> He's about as real as Longinus or Dracula, and more obscure than either as a vampiric figure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}